{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-q-heat-equation","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:q-heat-equation","kind":"definition","title":"$q$-Heat equation","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-q-harmonic-form","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-substrate-radial-coordinate"],"tags":["q-laplacian","heat-equation","reeb-flow","evolution"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.QHeatEquation","text":"q-heat-equation.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-heat-equation.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:q-heat-equation\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, \\varTheta, G, \\mathcal{S})</code> be a quantum observable universe with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-Laplacian <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Delta_q</code>. The <strong><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-heat equation</strong> is the evolution equation</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\partial_t u \\;=\\; -\\Delta_q u</code></pre>\n<p>for a time-dependent section <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">u \\colon \\mathbb{R}_{\\ge 0} \\times \\mathcal{S} \\to \\mathbf{1}_{\\mathbf{C}}</code>, where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">t</code> is the Reeb-flow parameter evaluated in units of the Planck step <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">t_P(q) = q/(q - 1)</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-heat-equation.md","heading":"Definition","number":"3.20.1"}
